From 090d7df3416c714c7f95bb366e61a111fe9c6cc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:50:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(verify): a Face row through a rim vertex crosses the rim

A stock-source Face whose last row ran exactly through two vertices on
the stock outline's straight sides (y 60 on a -2..62 stock) crossed no
edge interior, so the Boundary wall reading with no model read it as a
move inside the region and convicted its tangent pass with a Gouge -
no part in the document, and the post refused the program.

The no-model branch of wall_gouge now counts a pass through a loop
vertex whose two neighbours stand on opposite sides of the trace as a
rim crossing (Trace::through, for segments, XY arcs and plane-arc
footprints). A touch at a vertex, a move inside the region near a wall,
and every cut into a part (keep law, solid law) are still refused.

Pinned by face_stock_edge (app) and boundary_walls (sim).

Fixes #1659

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
